---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site.mjs';

const analytics = Boolean(site.analyticsId);
// Everything the site keeps in the browser's local storage: [key, what it is for, how long].
const stored: [string, string, string][] = [
  ['cookieConsent', 'Your Accept or Reject choice from the cookie banner (only saved if the banner is shown and you choose).', '180 days'],
];
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="How Fiction & Fact Library handles your data: no accounts, no ads, no personal details, anonymous statistics, and what stays in your browser." section="" crumbs={[['Privacy policy']]}>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <div class="page-intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Fiction & Fact Library is built for students. We don’t have accounts, we never ask for names or email addresses, we show no ads, and the tools save nothing about who you are.</p>
      <p class="muted">Last updated November 13, 2026.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>No accounts, no personal details</h2>
    <p>You can use every tool, worksheet and answer key without signing up. The tools run in your browser: what you type, paste or answer is not sent to us.</p>

    <h2>No ads</h2>
    <p>The site shows no ads and uses no advertising cookies.</p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    {analytics ? (
      <p>We use Google Analytics 4 to count visits and see which tools are used, so we can improve them. It records anonymous, aggregated information such as pages viewed, the type of device and browser, the approximate country, and tool events such as “a round was finished” with the level and the score. It never receives names or any text that students type or paste. Google processes this data as described in <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a>.</p>
    ) : (
      <p>Fiction & Fact Library does not run any analytics at the moment, so no analytics cookies are set.</p>
    )}

    <h2>Cookie choices</h2>
    {analytics ? (
      <p>Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland see a small banner and choose Accept or Reject before any analytics cookies are used. Your choice is remembered for 180 days, and you can change it any time with <strong>Cookie settings</strong> at the bottom of every page. Elsewhere, anonymous statistics are on by default.</p>
    ) : (
      <p>Because the site currently uses no analytics, it sets no cookies and shows no cookie banner.</p>
    )}

    <h2>What is stored in your browser</h2>
    <p>The site may keep a few small values in your browser’s local storage. They stay on your device and are never sent to us.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">What it is for</th><th scope="col">How long</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {stored.map(([key, purpose, time]) => <tr><td><code>{key}</code></td><td>{purpose}</td><td>{time}</td></tr>)}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Fonts and hosting</h2>
    <p>The site is served by Cloudflare, which processes standard request data (such as IP addresses) to deliver and protect the site. Text is set in fonts loaded from Google Fonts, which receives your IP address when the fonts are downloaded.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The tools are designed for students aged about 7 to 14 and do not collect personal information from anyone. Teachers can use them in class without collecting any student data.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>
